1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,008
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,961
HIERARCHY

3
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:47,047
[music fades]

4
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,760
[tender music playing]

5
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,237
[Woo-jin] Mmm.

6
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:16,910
[Woo-jin moans]

7
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:21,247
Good morning. You sleep all right?

8
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:24,084
[chuckles] Mm-mm.

9
00:01:27,128 --> 00:01:28,171
[Woo-jin moans]

10
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:33,384
Time to wake up.

11
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:35,303
[Woo-jin] Mm-mm.

12
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:38,473
[kisses]

13
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:43,478
Did you sleep all right?

14
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,188
[woman] Mmm.

15
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,691
[distant train horn blares]

16
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:00,537
Don't be late, okay?

17
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:04,082
[Woo-jin chuckles]

18
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:07,043
-[Woo-jin] I'll see you at school.
-See ya!

19
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:16,761
[pensive music playing]

20
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:31,651
EPISODE 2
SECRET: WITHIN A SECRET

21
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:36,656
[pensive music continues]

22
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,454
-We're finished.
-[engines roaring]

23
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:44,664
I'm done. [echoes]

24
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,374
[pensive music continues]

25
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:50,920
[exhales forcefully]

26
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:56,926
[stirring music playing]

27
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:08,938
[operatic music playing]

28
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:20,408
[music continues muffled]

29
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:23,494
[music continues as normal]

30
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:33,171
[music continues muffled]

31
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:36,257
[music continues as normal]

32
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,594
[music fades]

33
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:25,098
I trust you've all been well.
Hand out their gifts.

34
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,146
We're very grateful, ma'am.

35
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:35,984
[Ri-an] I didn't think
I'd see you until next month.

36
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:40,196
Ri-an, my dear son.

37
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,948
You're looking well.

38
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:44,617
My business in Singapore ended early,
so I thought I'd visit.

39
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,995
How's school? A third-year already!

40
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:51,332
My, how time flies.
You'll be in college before we know it.

41
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,127
A mother gets emotional.

42
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,837
They grow up so fast.

43
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:57,797
I'm a second-year.

44
00:04:58,631 --> 00:04:59,465
Hmm?

45
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,592
I still have a year before I graduate.

46
00:05:03,469 --> 00:05:06,806
That's wonderful! Have you thought about
what university you'd like to attend?

47
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:09,684
Perhaps… England would be a good fit?

48
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:10,685
Oh.

49
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:13,021
Let's get my schedule in order.

50
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:14,188
Yes, ma'am.

51
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:15,898
[pensive music playing]

52
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:22,572
Lunch with the executives at 12:00.

53
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:24,449
Jooshin Gallery at 2:00.

54
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:25,658
Jooshin Hotel at 4:00.

55
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:28,036
And… what else was there?

56
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:29,746
[man] You have a meeting with Director An.

57
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,874
-I'll squeeze the director in after lunch.
-[man] Right.

58
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,585
[mother] Everything in London
is marvelous, except the weather.

59
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:38,588
Choose somewhere in the UK.
You won't regret it.

60
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:40,173
[Ri-an] You've been gone three months.

61
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:42,216
We haven't had a real conversation
in over a year.

62
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:45,178
You could at least ask me how I'm doing.

63
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:48,097
Like, if I'm eating all right,
or if I've been sick!

64
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:49,390
I'm not a grown-up.

65
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,643
I still need my parents sometimes.

66
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:55,897
How many staff members
have I assigned to take care of Ri-an?

67
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,273
Six tutors, two assistants,

68
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:59,233
three health specialists,
and four nutritionists.

69
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:00,443
Fifteen total, ma'am.

70
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:03,321
What kind of attention are you lacking?

71
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:05,406
[breathes deeply]

72
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:15,583
And let's set something up with CEO Ryu
before the board meeting.

73
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:16,751
[man] Yes, ma'am.

74
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,725
[engine revving]

75
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:39,982
[sighs]

76
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:45,321
[indistinct chattering]

77
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:47,115
Oh! Tae-ho!

78
00:06:48,574 --> 00:06:49,450
Hey!

79
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,160
[indistinct chattering]

80
00:06:53,162 --> 00:06:54,705
[scoffs] Jesus Christ.

81
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:56,874
Get your dirty hands off me,
you charity case!

82
00:07:00,294 --> 00:07:01,546
[student 1] Hey, Tae-ho.

83
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:04,090
[pensive music playing]

84
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:08,094
[student 2 chuckles] Man,
you really don't have a clue, do you?

85
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:10,596
-Do you know Tae-ho?
-[student 3] Of course he doesn't.

86
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:13,433
Does he look like he's friends
with the heir to Jaeyul Hotels?

87
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:16,394
Look, scholarship kid,
going here doesn't make you our friend.

88
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,313
-[Ha laughs]
-[student 3] He laughed!

89
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:20,648
-Wow!
-[student 2] In our faces!

90
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:24,444
This commoner thinks he can just come up
and touch the nobles whenever he wants.

91
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:27,405
[student 2] Tae-ho should wash
his shoulder. It might start rotting off.

92
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:29,157
-[camera shutter clicking]
-Ooh, look.

93
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,241
Ooh!

94
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:31,993
[Ye-ji] No way!
He actually showed his face?

95
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:34,662
Ri-an's gonna make
an unboxing video with his guts.

96
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:38,332
He's got nerve, that's for sure.
Seriously, what was going on that night?

97
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:41,210
How could Jae-i just stand there
and let that scholarship kid kiss her?

98
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:42,420
Maybe she was into it.

99
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:45,089
[Ye-ji] Ugh, no way!
Jae-i with a scholarship kid?

100
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:47,341
She would never! Would she, He-ra?

101
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,220
I wouldn't rule it out.

102
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:54,765
Scholarship or not,
if Jae-i likes him, that's that.

103
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:55,933
Actually, it's inspiring.

104
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:59,979
To be attracted to someone without regard
to their status or social class.

105
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:00,980
[Ye-ji] Really?

106
00:08:01,063 --> 00:08:03,816
So what about you, He-ra?
Does that rule apply to you?

107
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:04,984
Oh, I'm different.

108
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:08,070
I could never be attracted to a man
that much poorer than I am.

109
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:10,364
It's just in my DNA.

110
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:12,408
Oh. Hey, he's coming.

111
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:15,036
[indistinct chattering]

112
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:42,647
[female student] You don't wanna get
on their bad side.

113
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,857
Everything Chan-min said
the other day is true.

114
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:45,942
The kid who died,

115
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,069
it was because he pissed off Ri-an.

116
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:50,238
They said it was a hit-and-run,
but that's bullshit.

117
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:53,282
He was so scared of Ri-an's goons,
he ran into traffic.

118
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,450
[intriguing music playing]

119
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:56,202
Or somebody hit him on purpose.

120
00:08:57,286 --> 00:09:00,122
[Ha] But why?
What did he do to piss off Ri-an?

121
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,166
[female student] It was because of Jae-i.

122
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,502
He was friends with Jae-i,
and Ri-an didn't like it.

123
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:07,630
-What? You mean, that's all?
-"That's all"? Jae-i's his girlfriend!

124
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:11,175
His Achilles heel.
She's the only thing he cares about!

125
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:13,511
[rhythmic pop music playing]

126
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:46,460
[Ri-an] Tell me something.

127
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:48,296
Was that little show really necessary?

128
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,630
What do you mean, "show"?

129
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:51,382
The kiss?

130
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,596
What I said earlier
should have been enough.

131
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,681
I've been perfectly clear to you.

132
00:09:59,223 --> 00:10:01,684
Who I like
and what I choose to do with them

133
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:03,644
has nothing to do with you.

134
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:04,812
You like that guy?

135
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:06,772
The scholarship kid?

136
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:10,192
What's really going on here?

137
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:13,279
What's the real reason
you're calling it off all of a sudden?

138
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,990
And why are you
bringing the new kid into it?

139
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:19,952
You said you'd die
before you told me the truth,

140
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,621
but I need to know, Jung Jae-i.

141
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,372
Matter of fact,

142
00:10:24,582 --> 00:10:26,667
I'm not letting you get away
without an explanation.

143
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:31,631
I can promise you right now
I'm willing to do whatever it takes.

144
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:37,094
Whatever it takes to find out
the secret you're keeping from me.

145
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:39,680
And I won't stop
until you're back were you belong.

146
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:47,813
[rhythmic pop music continues]

147
00:10:58,157 --> 00:11:00,493
I'll take care of that prick. Quietly.

148
00:11:00,576 --> 00:11:02,036
No, not quietly.

149
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:03,537
I want everybody to know.

150
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:07,083
He needs to learn
that there are consequences

151
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,335
for putting his hands on what's mine.

152
00:11:09,418 --> 00:11:11,629
Don't you think
we should lay low for a little while

153
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:13,047
when that other kid just died?

154
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:16,217
[music fades]

155
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,843
Okay, I'll take care of it.

156
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,470
He'll get the message.

157
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,767
[Yun-seok] From this moment on,

158
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,895
any asshole that speaks
to the new scholarship student,

159
00:11:27,978 --> 00:11:29,355
or even acknowledges him,

160
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:31,941
will get the same treatment.

161
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:33,943
Chan-min.

162
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:35,444
[Chan-min groaning in pain]

163
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:38,114
I shouldn't have to tell you
how to handle this stuff.

164
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:40,658
I mean, do I have to
hold your fucking hand through everything?

165
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:42,702
[Chan-min] You're right.
It won't happen again.

166
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,787
I was actually
just in the middle of a plan.

167
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,455
A plan to take care of him!

168
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:49,417
[Ha laughing]

169
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:54,255
[laughing continues]

170
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:55,548
I'm sorry.

171
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:59,009
I've never seen anyone make these plans
in front of their target.

172
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,052
[scoffs]

173
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,638
-Have you?
-Do you have a death wish, motherfucker?

174
00:12:02,722 --> 00:12:04,765
[pensive music playing]

175
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:08,018
Hey, Yun-seok just told you
not to speak to me.

176
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:09,353
Or did you not hear him?

177
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,147
You crazy fucker…

178
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:13,315
[Chan-min groaning]

179
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:15,526
[camera shutter clicks]

180
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:16,777
-[Ha] Chan-min!
-Hey!

181
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:20,114
If you should be hitting someone now,
it should be him instead of me, right?

182
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,240
Hmm?

183
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:23,159
[in pain] Ah! My fingers!

184
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:26,829
Shit! You son of a bitch!
Why are you all fucking standing there?

185
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:28,539
[Chan-min grunts in pain]

186
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:30,875
Ugh, this is fucking bullshit!

187
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:32,960
[Chan-min grunts, groans]

188
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:34,962
Asshole!

189
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,132
[woman] What do you think you're doing?

190
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:42,011
A third-year?

191
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:44,263
What are you doing down here?

192
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:47,600
[Chan-min] Shit! So fucking embarrassing!

193
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:49,685
[breathes deeply]

194
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:56,609
[woman] I have
a brief announcement to make.

195
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:59,612
This year's Healing Forest retreat
will go ahead as planned.

196
00:12:59,695 --> 00:13:02,239
All the details
will be posted in the group chat.

197
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,576
If you're unable to attend,
please notify me in advance.

198
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:07,828
That's all.

199
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:12,374
[sighs]

200
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,545
Jae-i.

201
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,425
Hang on. Can we talk for a minute?

202
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:25,679
Yeah.

203
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:28,933
Just say it.

204
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,309
Don't worry about her.

205
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:32,269
[clears throat]

206
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,356
You heard her.

207
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,237
I'm sorry… about the other night.

208
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,492
-I'm sorry if what I did offended you--
-Scholarship kid.

209
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:47,785
Kang Ha. That's my name.

210
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:51,121
Not "scholarship kid." Kang Ha.

211
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,874
Whatever your name is,
we were just fooling around at a party.

212
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:56,418
That's it. I hate it when guys get clingy.

213
00:13:57,628 --> 00:14:00,005
Oh, do you want some advice?

214
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:02,800
I'm paying you back
for the shirt you lent me the other day.

215
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:09,932
Drop out.

216
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:11,016
"Drop out"?

217
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,477
Why should I drop out now?

218
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:17,189
Ri-an hates you, so that's the only thing
you can do to defend yourself.

219
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,359
[Ha] Ah.

220
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:23,529
If it's about that,
I can take care of myself.

221
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:24,613
And also…

222
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:27,491
[chuckles] …I liked kissing you.

223
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,370
I liked that it was you.

224
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,789
And I really liked that you didn't

225
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:35,457
push me away.

226
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:39,336
[chuckles]

227
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:41,130
[Jae-i scoffs]

228
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:45,551
[chuckles softly]

229
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:46,760
[He-ra] I'm rooting for you,

230
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:49,013
this passionate romance
between the classes.

231
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:54,018
But what made you choose Jae-i?
There were plenty of girls there.

232
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:55,269
She was pretty.

233
00:14:55,352 --> 00:14:56,353
What?

234
00:14:58,230 --> 00:14:59,440
She was the prettiest.

235
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:00,941
That night.

236
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:03,819
Out of every girl there.

237
00:15:04,695 --> 00:15:05,654
[chuckles softly]

238
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:08,574
[acoustic guitar music playing]

239
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:09,700
That's it?

240
00:15:11,785 --> 00:15:15,247
You put your life on the line
all because she was… cute?

241
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,542
[scoffs]

242
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:20,628
[acoustic guitar music continues]

243
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:32,097
[Ri-an] I mean,
I thought I had to do something.

244
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,098
I'm sorry.

245
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:35,017
Whatever I did,

246
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:37,561
I'm sorry for everything.

247
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,647
[poignant pop music playing]

248
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:50,491
[Jae-i laughs on video]

249
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,744
[Jae-i] How do I look? Pretty cool, huh?

250
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:56,330
[Ri-an] It suits you.

251
00:15:56,413 --> 00:15:58,332
Hop in. I'll give you a ride somewhere.

252
00:15:58,415 --> 00:16:00,209
-[Jae-i laughs]
-[Ri-an] Shall we?

253
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,173
[chuckles]

254
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,135
[Ri-an] Got you on camera.

255
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:11,595
-[Ri-an laughs]
-Ah!

256
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,972
[laughing]

257
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:14,974
[Jae-i laughs]

258
00:16:27,861 --> 00:16:29,238
[Ri-an] What are you eating?

259
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:31,699
-[Jae-i] Ice cream.
-All to yourself? You're not gonna share?

260
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:33,033
Here. Here, have some.

261
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:35,953
-[Ri-an] Ah!
-Ah.

262
00:16:36,578 --> 00:16:38,497
I'm gonna need you a little closer.

263
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,249
-[Jae-i] Give it to me. [laughs]
-Ah!

264
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:42,459
[Jae-i] Seriously! Hey!

265
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:43,502
Enough!

266
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:44,753
[both laughing]

267
00:16:45,462 --> 00:16:47,172
-[Jae-i] Hey, hey.
-[Ri-an moans playfully]

268
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:48,841
-[Jae-i] Hey!
-[Ri-an screams playfully]

269
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:50,467
[Ri-an groaning]

270
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:53,012
Are you sorry?
Don't mess with people's food.

271
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,597
Ice cream or me?

272
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,598
Ice cream.

273
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:58,517
Huh? Get back here.

274
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:00,853
Now you're in for it.

275
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,356
Say "ah!"

276
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,316
Come on, open wide!
I can't reach that far.

277
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,986
-Ah!
-[Jei-i] Ah-- Hey!

278
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:10,070
That was your fault!

279
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:12,156
-[Ri-an] You're right. It's my fault.
-You admit it?

280
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:13,115
[Ri-an] I admit it.

281
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:14,950
-But one thing.
-What?

282
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:15,868
[door opens]

283
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:18,454
[Ri-an] Are you willing
to beat up your boyfriend over ice cream?

284
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:20,748
-[Jae-i] Well, you deserved it.
-Ice cream or me. Choose.

285
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:22,624
-[Jae-i] Well, it's obvious…
-[Ri-an] Oh yeah?

286
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:24,293
-[Jae-i] I choose…
-[Ri-an] Yes?

287
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,170
-[Jae-i] Ice cream.
-Not gonna cry, are you?

288
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:27,713
-[Ri-an] Come here.
-[Jae-i laughs]

289
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:30,507
-[Ri-an] Seriously, come here!
-Aren't you just a hopeless romantic?

290
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:32,676
You know, this is a bit of a turnoff.

291
00:17:34,595 --> 00:17:36,096
[music fades]

292
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:39,975
I saw Jae-i outside the hotel.

293
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:42,061
[pensive music playing]

294
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:50,778
Are you even listening to me?
Stop moping. It's gross.

295
00:17:51,403 --> 00:17:52,279
Cut it out.

296
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:54,907
Remember, Jae-i hates it
when guys get too clingy.

297
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:03,916
I know something you can try.

298
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:06,293
What are you thinking?

299
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,796
Try dating someone else.

300
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:13,634
Since you were 15-- No, even longer.

301
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:14,968
Ever since you guys were six,

302
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:17,513
you've never given any other girl
so much as a second glance.

303
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:19,890
Seeing you with someone else
would drive her crazy.

304
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:22,226
I know if it were me, I'd want you back.

305
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:24,686
So I should date someone else
to lure her back?

306
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:27,022
Yeah. Or pretend to. Just be convincing.

307
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,149
Poor girl.

308
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:31,568
I'm sure she still has feelings for you.

309
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:33,362
Why else would she drive out here?

310
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:36,907
You need to get smart about this soon
if you're serious about winning her back.

311
00:18:37,407 --> 00:18:38,575
This is your only shot.

312
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:40,494
[inhales deeply]

313
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:41,578
Well then…

314
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:47,251
you should

315
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:49,795
look into something.

316
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:54,591
Look into what, exactly?

317
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:56,927
The reason that she's leaving.

318
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:58,929
The real reason.

319
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:06,270
I don't think I can.

320
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:10,691
No one wants you back together
more than I do, but I'm her best friend.

321
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,192
I can't start spying on her, can I?

322
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:23,412
[melodic pop music playing]

323
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:50,480
-[Woo-jin] Been a while.
-Good to see you.

324
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:53,358
[Woo-jin] Just tell me, already.

325
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:56,445
Tell you what?

326
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:58,197
We both know you have a secret.

327
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:00,908
Why suffer through it alone?

328
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:02,743
You can share.

329
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:06,038
[phone buzzing]

330
00:20:08,832 --> 00:20:10,167
Let me take this.

331
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:13,420
Looks like I'm not
the only one with a secret.

332
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:14,755
What happened to sharing?

333
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:19,259
I'll be right back.

334
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,893
[phone buzzes]

335
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:33,607
[mysterious music playing]

336
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:35,484
[distorted male voice]
If you keep ignoring me,

337
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,070
I'll consider sending this
to your father too.

338
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:39,613
[echoes] …your father too.

339
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,829
This is the email address
for the secretary's office

340
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,122
at Jaeyul Group, right?

341
00:20:51,667 --> 00:20:54,002
[Jae-i breathes nervously]

342
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:58,298
[sighs]

343
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,259
[computer beeping]

344
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:11,019
[In-han] You said you took care of it.

345
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:13,522
You deleted everything, right?
So what's the problem?

346
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:15,607
[grunts]

347
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:16,608
[item clatters]

348
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:18,694
[Jae-i breathing anxiously]

349
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:22,864
[Jae-i whimpers]

350
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:24,825
[In-han] You're positive?

351
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:26,868
You're sure you did?

352
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:27,953
Yes, I'm sure.

353
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:31,290
I checked twice.
No, three times. I'm absolutely sure.

354
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,125
What do I do now?

355
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:35,127
What's gonna happen to me?
What the hell do I do?

356
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,211
[Jae-i whimpers]

357
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,839
Don't worry, we'll find a way.

358
00:21:38,922 --> 00:21:40,424
No, it's too late for that.

359
00:21:40,507 --> 00:21:41,842
I did everything I could.

360
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:46,263
-[In-han] Jae-i.
-You have no idea.

361
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:47,806
You don't know what my dad is like.

362
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:52,060
When he finds out,
he'll hide me away like my mom.

363
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:53,562
Or he'll just kill me.

364
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:56,606
At this point,

365
00:21:57,357 --> 00:22:00,944
it'd be better if I just…
if I just died before it gets out.

366
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:02,321
We'll figure something out.

367
00:22:02,821 --> 00:22:03,989
I can help you.

368
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,074
[sobs] I'm so scared

369
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:08,118
I'll end up like my mom!

370
00:22:08,201 --> 00:22:10,078
I'm scared that my dad will kill me!

371
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,580
[Jae-i sobs]

372
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:19,838
[sniffles]

373
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:23,342
Wait.

374
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:27,179
[tense music playing]

375
00:22:27,929 --> 00:22:28,889
Don't tell me…

376
00:22:28,972 --> 00:22:31,141
[student 1] Jae-i? What? Hey! Hey!

377
00:22:32,184 --> 00:22:33,602
-What are you doing in here?
-Jae-i!

378
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:36,104
-[student 1] Get out before we beat you.
-Jae-i! Wait, please!

379
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,314
-Jae-i!
-[student 1] Get out!

380
00:22:40,525 --> 00:22:42,110
[tense music continues]

381
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:50,160
[male distorted voice] How about it?
Are you interested in speaking to me now?

382
00:22:53,914 --> 00:22:55,916
[melodic pop music playing]

383
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:00,545
[Woo-jin sighs]

384
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:07,052
[breathes deeply]

385
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:09,846
-You're leaving?
-Yeah.

386
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:11,723
I'm tired. See you later.

387
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:17,813
[gunshot echoes]

388
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:24,069
[Jae-hyeok exclaims]

389
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:25,862
You nearly had it! [laughs]

390
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:27,030
Close one, Dad.

391
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:43,338
-[phone buzzing]
-Chairman Jung.

392
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:46,299
[phone buzzing]

393
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:49,344
I said don't disturb me.

394
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:53,390
What?

395
00:23:53,473 --> 00:23:55,475
[stirring music playing]

396
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:00,605
What was uploaded?

397
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:04,151
[chuckles]

398
00:24:04,234 --> 00:24:06,361
Confirm the details and stand by for now.

399
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:12,868
[tense music playing]

400
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,706
Tell me it isn't true, Jung Jae-i.

401
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:25,213
No daughter of mine
could do something like that.

402
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:28,341
I'd expect this kind of thing
out of your filthy, low-class mother.

403
00:24:28,425 --> 00:24:30,469
But you? There's no way.

404
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:33,805
I refuse to believe
my daughter would humiliate me like this.

405
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:35,807
[gun clicks]

406
00:24:36,516 --> 00:24:37,517
Answer me.

407
00:24:38,101 --> 00:24:40,645
-Don't stand there gaping like a fool!
-[gun cocks]

408
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:42,272
[dog barking]

409
00:24:46,234 --> 00:24:48,445
-[laughing]
-Answer me right now!

410
00:24:51,698 --> 00:24:53,033
I'm afraid I have to go.

411
00:24:53,116 --> 00:24:55,118
-[tense music subsides]
-[Jae-i exhales]

412
00:24:57,787 --> 00:24:59,706
An issue has come up at work.

413
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:03,752
Oh really? It must be bad news.

414
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:06,463
Something odd was posted
on the board members' forum.

415
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:08,840
I have to assess the situation.

416
00:25:10,884 --> 00:25:13,553
I feel awful. We haven't been
hunting together for a while.

417
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,514
Now I've gone and ruined it.

418
00:25:17,349 --> 00:25:18,975
Don't rush coming back down.

419
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:23,188
[sighs, clears throat]

420
00:25:24,439 --> 00:25:25,524
[chuckles]

421
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:31,238
[sighs]

422
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:38,954
There we go. Now the lemon zest.

423
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:43,291
Director Jang called.
He's been trying to reach you all morning.

424
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,585
Everything's all right at work?

425
00:25:46,336 --> 00:25:47,754
Of course it is. We're fine.

426
00:25:48,421 --> 00:25:50,215
And have you heard back from Jooshin?

427
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,386
I told you not to worry.

428
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:57,681
Oh. Is it today already?

429
00:25:57,764 --> 00:26:00,642
Only the most special day of the year!

430
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:04,563
The day that I get to prepare
my daughter's breakfast myself!

431
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:05,689
[chuckles]

432
00:26:06,398 --> 00:26:07,357
[phone alert]

433
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:12,279
[Jae-i] Come see me at the house later.

434
00:26:14,197 --> 00:26:15,615
Am I your servant now?

435
00:26:18,159 --> 00:26:20,412
[student 1 laughs]
That shit is so funny, man.

436
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:22,622
[student 2] That's not the craziest part.
Later…

437
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:23,790
[student 3] Hey.

438
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:25,667
[student 2] Let's go.

439
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:28,670
[beeping]

440
00:26:48,023 --> 00:26:49,190
[locker door closes]

441
00:26:53,403 --> 00:26:55,447
-[unsettling music playing]
-[Ha sighs]

442
00:26:55,530 --> 00:26:57,324
[In-ha] They spiked my drink
with something.

443
00:26:58,700 --> 00:26:59,993
It had to be some kind of drug.

444
00:27:04,372 --> 00:27:05,624
I almost died.

445
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:07,375
I'm serious.

446
00:27:09,085 --> 00:27:13,048
Wait. In-han. Just try and calm down.
You think high school kids would do that?

447
00:27:13,131 --> 00:27:14,633
You have no idea

448
00:27:16,468 --> 00:27:18,136
what kind of place Jooshin is…

449
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:22,349
what kind of people they are.

450
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:26,061
[sighs in frustration]

451
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:38,365
[unsettling music continues]

452
00:27:40,283 --> 00:27:42,827
[Ri-an] Were your parent's fired
from Jooshin or something?

453
00:27:42,911 --> 00:27:44,913
Were they contractors
whose business dried up?

454
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:46,456
Who the hell are you?

455
00:27:47,082 --> 00:27:48,583
What's your deal, huh?

456
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:51,503
Everyone keeps telling me you're the one
who runs things around here.

457
00:27:52,545 --> 00:27:54,464
I'm only doing what I need to survive.

458
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,676
If I have to go up against you
to do that, so be it.

459
00:27:57,759 --> 00:27:58,802
That true?

460
00:28:00,011 --> 00:28:00,887
You sure?

461
00:28:07,435 --> 00:28:10,397
You see, I wanna know
what you're up to, scholarship kid.

462
00:28:12,023 --> 00:28:12,982
Try me.

463
00:28:15,235 --> 00:28:16,778
We'll see how long you last.

464
00:28:21,199 --> 00:28:23,493
[Ha] In-han was being bullied, assaulted,

465
00:28:24,452 --> 00:28:25,912
and Kim Ri-an was behind it.

466
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:29,582
Could he have spiked In-han's drink too?

467
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:30,750
[sighs]

468
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:43,096
[indistinct chattering]

469
00:28:46,891 --> 00:28:48,685
We need to deal with him
at the Healing Forest.

470
00:28:48,768 --> 00:28:50,645
If we wait any longer, we're dead!

471
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:53,690
But, Chan-min, he didn't even flinch
when you tried to hit him.

472
00:28:54,190 --> 00:28:56,401
How do we get
someone like that to drop out?

473
00:28:56,484 --> 00:28:58,236
We just have to kill his spirit!

474
00:28:58,319 --> 00:28:59,946
Either we kick his face in

475
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:02,699
or deal with him like Kang In-han,

476
00:29:03,199 --> 00:29:04,242
make him disappear.

477
00:29:05,034 --> 00:29:07,787
No one would bat an eye
if another lowlife died anyway.

478
00:29:07,871 --> 00:29:10,415
Get off your fucking phone
when I'm talking to you!

479
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:12,834
Ugh! These fucking idiots!

480
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:19,215
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

481
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:21,134
[door opens]

482
00:29:22,051 --> 00:29:23,094
[music fades]

483
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,095
[door closes]

484
00:29:34,105 --> 00:29:35,857
Ms. Han asked me to bring you this.

485
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:37,317
[woman] Mm-hmm.

486
00:29:38,485 --> 00:29:40,069
How's it going?

487
00:29:40,153 --> 00:29:41,446
And how is everyone?

488
00:29:42,405 --> 00:29:43,907
Who exactly do you mean by that?

489
00:29:43,990 --> 00:29:46,367
Ri-an, Jae-i, Woo-jin, He-ra.

490
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:48,203
I'm talking about your friends.

491
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:49,704
My friends?

492
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:52,665
They're all fine.

493
00:29:52,749 --> 00:29:54,834
[woman] Don't waste your time
with the wrong people.

494
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:57,504
The friends you make here
will last a lifetime.

495
00:29:58,254 --> 00:30:00,924
They'll be very helpful
when you start your career.

496
00:30:01,007 --> 00:30:02,926
You understand what I mean, don't you?

497
00:30:04,761 --> 00:30:05,804
Yes.

498
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:11,434
One thing, Mom.

499
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:14,813
How did you cover it up?

500
00:30:16,064 --> 00:30:17,690
[pensive music playing]

501
00:30:17,774 --> 00:30:19,234
In-han's death, I mean.

502
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:22,153
You made sure
there wasn't even a single article.

503
00:30:23,071 --> 00:30:24,197
I'm curious how.

504
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:28,785
I'm afraid I don't know
what you're talking about.

505
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:30,995
Go on, you'll be late.

506
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:43,591
-[sighs]
-[door opens]

507
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:46,594
[door closes]

508
00:30:49,722 --> 00:30:50,723
[Ha] You have to open it.

509
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:53,059
I saw Kim Ri-an put drugs
into Choi Yun-seok's locker.

510
00:30:53,142 --> 00:30:54,352
[music fades]

511
00:30:56,646 --> 00:30:59,983
[Ms. Han] It's against school policy
to open a student's personal locker.

512
00:31:00,066 --> 00:31:01,359
It's a breach of privacy.

513
00:31:01,442 --> 00:31:03,778
If you don't open it for me,
I'll file a formal complaint.

514
00:31:04,362 --> 00:31:06,739
A formal complaint? For?

515
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:10,159
You saw me being attacked
in the classroom, and you just ignored it.

516
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:12,537
[Ms. Han sighs]

517
00:31:13,413 --> 00:31:16,416
Kang Ha, a school is a tiny society.

518
00:31:16,499 --> 00:31:20,044
At Jooshin, we give students the freedom
to resolve minor issues amongst themselves

519
00:31:20,128 --> 00:31:22,088
to help them function within that society.

520
00:31:23,089 --> 00:31:24,841
Help us? Help us how?

521
00:31:24,924 --> 00:31:28,803
Help us learn respect for the bosses' sons
since they'll be our bosses in the future?

522
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:30,680
Help us remember we're poor,

523
00:31:30,763 --> 00:31:33,349
and that we'd better get used to
getting walked all over?

524
00:31:33,433 --> 00:31:36,352
That doesn't sound much like "help" to me.
Or does it to you?

525
00:31:36,436 --> 00:31:37,270
Kang Ha!

526
00:31:37,353 --> 00:31:39,522
Maybe I should let the press know
about my assault,

527
00:31:39,606 --> 00:31:41,691
about Jooshin's special rules.

528
00:31:41,774 --> 00:31:42,650
Everything.

529
00:32:00,043 --> 00:32:01,127
[Ms. Han sighs]

530
00:32:11,346 --> 00:32:13,681
[stirring music playing]

531
00:32:17,477 --> 00:32:18,561
[Ms. Han sighs]

532
00:32:23,066 --> 00:32:24,317
[tense music playing]

533
00:32:30,073 --> 00:32:31,032
[keypad beeps]

534
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:31,950
[Ba-da] Boo!

535
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:33,117
Oh, you scared me.

536
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:35,286
I'm so hungry. Buy me a yogurt?

537
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:36,496
-Yogurt?
-Mm-hmm.

538
00:32:37,038 --> 00:32:37,872
Come on.

539
00:32:37,956 --> 00:32:38,957
-Strawberry?
-Sure.

540
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:53,221
Is this it?
Is this what you were talking about?

541
00:32:53,304 --> 00:32:55,598
You see? We need an investigation.

542
00:32:55,682 --> 00:32:56,724
Find out what these are.

543
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:58,977
Find out who is dealing them
to who at school, and also,

544
00:33:00,228 --> 00:33:01,521
who they might have fed them to.

545
00:33:01,604 --> 00:33:03,022
This is Xanax.

546
00:33:03,856 --> 00:33:05,733
They're for anxiety disorders.

547
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:10,196
I don't know if these were prescribed
at your old school, but they are here.

548
00:33:10,279 --> 00:33:12,907
Most kids are under so much pressure,
they need them.

549
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:17,161
Go check with a police station
or hospital if you don't believe me.

550
00:33:21,082 --> 00:33:23,001
Just put it back before anyone finds out.

551
00:33:26,462 --> 00:33:27,672
And don't cause any trouble.

552
00:33:32,677 --> 00:33:33,803
[sighs in frustration]

553
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,305
[music fades]

554
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:42,020
[Jae-i] If someone's sending you
anonymous DMs,

555
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:43,771
can you find out who they are?

556
00:33:44,605 --> 00:33:45,648
I'm not sure.

557
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:47,108
Why do you ask?

558
00:33:47,191 --> 00:33:50,361
Well, you said you knew
a good harassment lawyer.

559
00:33:51,237 --> 00:33:52,697
Oh, yes, I do.

560
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:55,742
Eun-gyeong used this firm
to go after her Internet trolls.

561
00:33:56,534 --> 00:33:59,620
But the social media sites
don't like disclosing user info.

562
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:01,289
So it's hard to find out who's behind it.

563
00:34:01,372 --> 00:34:03,916
You know, I don't really care
if it's legal or not.

564
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:06,669
Just find someone
who can track anonymous accounts.

565
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:10,882
How would I do that though?

566
00:34:12,133 --> 00:34:14,844
I imagine way more people
are in your circle--

567
00:34:14,927 --> 00:34:16,721
You remember Woo-jin's birthday?

568
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:19,432
Someone took a video.

569
00:34:19,515 --> 00:34:21,559
-[intriguing music playing]
-Sorry, what?

570
00:34:21,642 --> 00:34:23,478
And that someone still has it too.

571
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:24,562
Wait.

572
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:27,106
Wait. Who has it?

573
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:29,067
Wait, why? And how? What was recorded?

574
00:34:30,026 --> 00:34:31,486
Was there anything bad in particular?

575
00:34:31,569 --> 00:34:33,696
Was there anything
that happened at that party

576
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:35,114
that you'd want recorded

577
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:38,284
and shared with everyone?

578
00:34:42,872 --> 00:34:45,583
Do whatever it takes.
I need to expose this account.

579
00:34:52,381 --> 00:34:54,050
[Ye-ji] Hey, how's this one?

580
00:34:56,094 --> 00:34:58,888
-Yeah, looks good.
-[Ye-ji] Should I choose one more?

581
00:34:58,971 --> 00:35:01,140
How long is this year's
Healing Forest retreat again?

582
00:35:01,224 --> 00:35:02,350
[Ba-da] It's a day, right?

583
00:35:02,433 --> 00:35:04,143
What was that guy's name?

584
00:35:05,269 --> 00:35:06,312
Kang…

585
00:35:07,980 --> 00:35:09,398
That kid who died?

586
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:10,608
Kang In-han?

587
00:35:10,691 --> 00:35:12,777
He died the day of
Woo-jin's birthday party, didn't he?

588
00:35:12,860 --> 00:35:14,278
Yeah, he did. You're right.

589
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:17,990
[crowd cheering, laughing]

590
00:35:19,242 --> 00:35:21,244
[cheering, laughing continues]

591
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:32,505
[intriguing music continues]

592
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:41,764
[sighs]

593
00:35:49,814 --> 00:35:51,941
This is Yoon He-ra. How have you been?

594
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,360
I need your help with something.

595
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:57,655
[rhythmic pop music playing]

596
00:36:17,884 --> 00:36:20,261
[rhythmic pop music continues]

597
00:36:27,768 --> 00:36:29,145
[woman 1] Everybody, listen up.

598
00:36:29,228 --> 00:36:31,981
We are about to begin
today's floating session.

599
00:36:32,064 --> 00:36:34,525
Relax your body and slowly lay back.

600
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:37,236
[rhythmic pop music continues]

601
00:36:41,741 --> 00:36:43,659
[woman 2] Take a deep breath in.

602
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:45,286
Inhale.

603
00:36:45,369 --> 00:36:46,329
[bowl resonates]

604
00:36:56,839 --> 00:36:58,174
Good shot!

605
00:36:58,257 --> 00:36:59,258
[both laugh]

606
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:01,344
-[music fades]
-[grunts, laughs]

607
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:08,809
-[camera shutter clicks]
-I haven't seen that kid today.

608
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:10,645
-Have you guys?
-I saw him earlier.

609
00:37:11,979 --> 00:37:15,274
What do you think, guys? Is this it?
Kang Ha's last night on earth?

610
00:37:15,358 --> 00:37:16,400
Oh, tonight?

611
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:19,195
I assume Chan-min
and the scholarship students wanna live.

612
00:37:19,278 --> 00:37:21,739
-So they've got something planned.
-It better be something good.

613
00:37:21,822 --> 00:37:22,823
Let's make it interesting.

614
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,325
Hey, Tae-ho, wanna bet on it?

615
00:37:24,408 --> 00:37:25,952
[chuckles] Bet what?

616
00:37:26,035 --> 00:37:27,995
I'll bet a million won
on the scholarship kid.

617
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:29,956
I bet he's stubborn enough to survive.

618
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:32,166
Me too. A million won
he makes it to tomorrow.

619
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,710
Oh. My million won says
he doesn't last the night.

620
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:36,170
A deal is a deal. All right, guys?

621
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:38,547
Park Tae-ho? How do you bet?

622
00:37:41,968 --> 00:37:43,302
I also bet a million he doesn't.

623
00:37:43,386 --> 00:37:45,846
Okay! That's two million if you lose.

624
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,682
-[Ye-ji] Yeah? Make it five.
-[Yun-seok] Five?

625
00:37:47,765 --> 00:37:49,558
I raise you five more. Now it's ten.

626
00:37:50,810 --> 00:37:54,105
Just pretend you're on a normal trip
with a normal school. This is your room.

627
00:37:54,605 --> 00:37:57,275
These are more tucked away,
better for the scholarship students.

628
00:37:57,358 --> 00:37:58,192
[Ha] Okay.

629
00:37:58,276 --> 00:38:01,028
Sign up at the information desk
for any sessions you want.

630
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:04,073
My advice.

631
00:38:04,573 --> 00:38:06,784
Do yourself a favor,
and choose the least popular ones.

632
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:08,661
We'll see. Thanks, man.

633
00:38:09,328 --> 00:38:10,955
This doesn't make us friends.

634
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:13,749
Don't talk to me in front of the others.

635
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:16,669
There's a reason they call me "Moss."

636
00:38:17,503 --> 00:38:18,963
My existence is barely noticed.

637
00:38:19,547 --> 00:38:22,174
-That's a shitty name to call someone.
-I'm not offended by it.

638
00:38:24,552 --> 00:38:26,929
I've worked hard for a long time
to earn that nickname.

639
00:38:27,722 --> 00:38:28,764
I'm not about to ruin it.

640
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:31,892
Not for anyone.

641
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:37,565
Well, thanks for the advice.

642
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:44,322
[soothing music playing]

643
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:53,664
[door closes]

644
00:38:53,748 --> 00:38:55,875
I've started looking into your problem.

645
00:38:55,958 --> 00:38:59,211
You know, whoever's behind this account,
if they were at the party with us,

646
00:38:59,295 --> 00:39:01,464
that probably means it's someone we know.

647
00:39:02,089 --> 00:39:05,092
You'd think our friends would know better
than to try pulling this shit on us.

648
00:39:05,176 --> 00:39:06,052
What do they want?

649
00:39:06,886 --> 00:39:08,179
I don't know.

650
00:39:08,262 --> 00:39:09,764
They never actually said.

651
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:12,641
Maybe they're hoping to make a buck
by threatening to make it public.

652
00:39:12,725 --> 00:39:15,311
But who at the party
would be so desperate or stupid enough

653
00:39:15,394 --> 00:39:17,104
to try and blackmail us for money?

654
00:39:17,772 --> 00:39:21,025
Send me those DMs when you get a chance.
I'll get someone on it.

655
00:39:24,945 --> 00:39:27,239
I'll send the messages on my own.

656
00:39:31,786 --> 00:39:33,913
[He-ra] You must be
in serious trouble, Jae-i.

657
00:39:34,413 --> 00:39:37,833
You weren't the only one filmed doing
something you shouldn't have been doing.

658
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:39,835
[door opens]

659
00:39:40,336 --> 00:39:41,545
[knocking at door]

660
00:39:42,338 --> 00:39:43,339
Brunch, anyone?

661
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:53,849
[Woo-jin sighs]

662
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:55,643
I haven't even touched my food,

663
00:39:56,769 --> 00:39:57,937
but my appetite's gone.

664
00:39:58,521 --> 00:40:01,690
-Could it be the vibes?
-Yeah, and I think it's contagious.

665
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:02,942
Because I feel the same way.

666
00:40:03,734 --> 00:40:05,778
[Woo-jin] It's been forever
since we all hung out.

667
00:40:05,861 --> 00:40:07,279
Can't you get along for one day?

668
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:08,406
[sighs]

669
00:40:10,074 --> 00:40:11,325
I'm gonna head out.

670
00:40:13,619 --> 00:40:16,580
Stay. You said you wanted to be friends.

671
00:40:18,541 --> 00:40:20,334
There's no reason to avoid me
if you meant it.

672
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,128
Don't you remember what you told me?

673
00:40:22,211 --> 00:40:25,047
That you would do "whatever it takes"
to try and get us back together.

674
00:40:30,928 --> 00:40:33,347
That's reason enough, don't you think?

675
00:40:37,309 --> 00:40:38,185
Hey, Jae-i!

676
00:40:39,603 --> 00:40:40,938
Wait. I'll walk you back!

677
00:40:44,233 --> 00:40:45,359
[sighs]

678
00:40:51,198 --> 00:40:52,199
So my plan.

679
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:53,826
You thought about it?

680
00:40:54,410 --> 00:40:55,327
[sighs]

681
00:40:56,328 --> 00:40:59,165
Forget about the plan, He-ra.
It'll never work.

682
00:40:59,248 --> 00:41:02,001
Jae-i would see through
a fake relationship in a second.

683
00:41:02,668 --> 00:41:05,296
-She'd know.
-With the right girl, she might not.

684
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:07,590
I'll do it.

685
00:41:09,675 --> 00:41:11,760
You? Why? What makes you
so perfect for the job?

686
00:41:12,553 --> 00:41:14,763
It has to be someone Jae-i would believe,

687
00:41:14,847 --> 00:41:18,642
but also someone who's willing to back off
the moment she starts to get jealous.

688
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:20,060
Trust me. I'm your only option.

689
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:23,439
I wasn't going to tell you this,

690
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:27,026
but even though
Jae-i still has feelings for you,

691
00:41:27,109 --> 00:41:29,028
she's crushing on the scholarship kid.

692
00:41:32,364 --> 00:41:34,867
I can clearly tell
just from the look in her eyes.

693
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:36,577
If you don't do something fast,

694
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:38,621
it'll be too late to ever win her back.

695
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:45,628
[sighs]

696
00:41:58,390 --> 00:41:59,266
[sighs]

697
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:04,146
[Ms. Han] I thought I packed all the meds,
but I forgot to bring any antacids.

698
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:06,232
Three boxes should be plenty.

699
00:42:10,569 --> 00:42:11,737
Kang Ha.

700
00:42:12,363 --> 00:42:15,241
I chose you for this
to help you avoid the other students.

701
00:42:16,158 --> 00:42:17,660
Well, thanks, I guess.

702
00:42:17,743 --> 00:42:20,454
Call me cowardly if you want,
but that's how this place works.

703
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:23,749
All I can do
is try to make the best of the situation.

704
00:42:23,832 --> 00:42:25,459
You don't need to explain it to me.

705
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:28,712
This place is just cowardly adults
afraid of insane children.

706
00:42:29,213 --> 00:42:31,048
I'm not even curious why anymore.

707
00:42:38,931 --> 00:42:39,807
[sighs]

708
00:42:45,854 --> 00:42:47,356
-Whoa!
-[brakes squeal]

709
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:48,524
Hey.

710
00:42:48,607 --> 00:42:51,235
Jesus! You startled me!
I nearly ran you over!

711
00:42:52,736 --> 00:42:54,863
-Are you going somewhere?
-Uh-huh.

712
00:42:55,447 --> 00:42:57,074
On an errand to the drugstore.

713
00:43:00,035 --> 00:43:02,246
Go on. I need to get more cigarettes.

714
00:43:02,329 --> 00:43:03,497
What?

715
00:43:04,164 --> 00:43:06,000
What? You want me to pedal?

716
00:43:08,836 --> 00:43:11,505
-[pensive music playing]
-[He-ra] Huh? Isn't that Jae-i?

717
00:43:15,259 --> 00:43:17,595
Yep, that's her with the scholarship kid.

718
00:43:18,554 --> 00:43:19,597
[Ha] Hold on.

719
00:43:30,357 --> 00:43:31,191
[sighs]

720
00:43:32,860 --> 00:43:33,861
[chuckles softly]

721
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:36,655
[romantic music playing]

722
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:00,638
[sighs] Feels good.

723
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:04,558
Hmm? What's that? I didn't hear.

724
00:44:05,100 --> 00:44:07,853
Ah. You like the beach? Wanna stop by?

725
00:44:08,646 --> 00:44:10,773
It's fine. Just keep going.

726
00:44:12,191 --> 00:44:13,067
Sure.

727
00:44:15,653 --> 00:44:18,864
[romantic music continues]

728
00:44:50,646 --> 00:44:51,897
[music fades]

729
00:45:06,829 --> 00:45:07,913
You want this?

730
00:45:09,456 --> 00:45:10,791
No, thanks. I'm fine.

731
00:45:16,130 --> 00:45:17,256
[Ha sighs]

732
00:45:18,048 --> 00:45:19,925
I don't think it'll let up anytime soon.

733
00:45:26,098 --> 00:45:26,932
[dog whimpers]

734
00:45:28,392 --> 00:45:29,435
-Aw.
-[dog barks]

735
00:45:30,561 --> 00:45:31,562
[Jae-i chuckles]

736
00:45:31,645 --> 00:45:32,980
You're so cute.

737
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:35,774
[gentle music playing]

738
00:45:39,153 --> 00:45:40,654
Ah! [laughs]

739
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:47,536
You're pretty.

740
00:45:48,912 --> 00:45:49,747
What?

741
00:45:51,498 --> 00:45:53,083
You know, you're pretty when you laugh.

742
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:56,837
I've never even seen you smile before.

743
00:45:57,838 --> 00:45:58,714
[dog whimpers]

744
00:45:59,506 --> 00:46:00,591
[Jae-i clears throat]

745
00:46:01,216 --> 00:46:02,259
[chuckles]

746
00:46:03,844 --> 00:46:05,095
I don't understand it.

747
00:46:05,971 --> 00:46:07,556
You're pretty, smart, popular,

748
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:10,434
and rich enough to have
whatever you want in your life.

749
00:46:11,268 --> 00:46:12,478
You got everything.

750
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:14,521
But you never smile.

751
00:46:15,606 --> 00:46:16,732
[inhales deeply]

752
00:46:16,815 --> 00:46:18,692
That's just the way I was raised.

753
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:23,071
I was taught to conceal my emotions
around others.

754
00:46:23,822 --> 00:46:26,033
"Laughter today becomes gossip tomorrow."

755
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:28,118
"And if anyone sees you cry,

756
00:46:28,786 --> 00:46:31,246
it's only a matter of time
before they use it against you."

757
00:46:32,289 --> 00:46:34,166
Wait. That's how they raised you?

758
00:46:35,083 --> 00:46:37,169
Mm-hmm. From the age of three.

759
00:46:38,796 --> 00:46:40,005
Wow. [chuckles]

760
00:46:40,589 --> 00:46:43,217
The rich really aren't
like the rest of us, are they?

761
00:46:46,136 --> 00:46:47,179
What about you?

762
00:46:47,262 --> 00:46:49,348
Everyone's always bullying you
for being poor.

763
00:46:49,431 --> 00:46:51,225
What do you have to smile about
all the time?

764
00:46:52,100 --> 00:46:52,935
What?

765
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:54,728
Who says I'm poor?

766
00:46:55,562 --> 00:46:57,397
[laughs] That's funny.

767
00:46:57,481 --> 00:47:00,067
I never thought of myself
as being poor or unhappy.

